Z||000000||2xsess||12-19-2000||01:28 AM||||I was watching the weather channel tonight, trying to keep an eye out to see what I'll be driving through on the way to NC this weekend. They have predicted that tomorrow it will snow in Savannah, now it won't be any accumilation but I would have never dreamed I'd hear it. Being from PA originally I'd love to see it snow a foot here just to see all these fools trying to get anywhere in it. I've heard that it snowed 2" here in 1989 and the whole area shut down for 2 days. <P>Let it snow let it snow  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroLisa||12-19-2000||01:32 AM||||I hope it doesn't snow here for two reasons: People will start rushing to the stores to stock up on supplies and start driving like idiots  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Im in NC right now, and it was almost warm today, I can't imagine it being snowing tomorrow. Its funny to see how all you southerners react to a snow prediction  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
